ernships and industry placements\nEmployability and careers\nContact\nApply for a higher degree by research\nHome\nStudy\nHigher degree by research\nTo apply for a higher degree by research (HDR) with us, you must find a supervisor and then apply online.\nFind and contact a supervisor\nYou can find a potential supervisor in three ways:\nVisit our research strengths pages to find an academic who shares your interest.\nVisit our people pages if you know the academic you\u2019d like to approach to supervise you.\nEmail our Graduate Research Coordinator at hdr.scmb@enquire.uq.edu.au if you\u2019d like help identifying a potential supervisor.\nWhen you contact your potential supervisor, keep your message succinct but include key information such as academic transcripts, CV, publications and details of any relevant experience or skills. Make it clear how their research aligns with your interest area.\nApply online\nOnce you have identified a potential supervisor, visit the UQ Graduate School's how-to-apply pages to submit your online application.\nApply for a higher degree by research\nUQ acknowledges the Traditional Owners and their custodianship of the lands on which UQ is situated. Reconciliation at UQ\nMedia\nMedia team contacts\nFind a subject matter expert\nUQ News\nWorking with us\nCareers and job search\nStrategic Plan\nStaff Intranet\nIT support\nCurrent students\nmy.UQ\nPrograms and courses\nAcademic calendar\nStudent support\nIT support\nLibrary\nLibrary\nStudy and learning support\nResearch and publish\nVisit\nContact\nContact UQ\nMake a complaint\nFaculties, schools, institutes and centres\nDivisions and departments\nCampuses, maps and transport\nMedia\nMedia team contacts\nFind a subject matter expert\nUQ News\nWorking with us\nCareers and job search\nStrategic Plan\nStaff Intranet\nIT support\nCurrent students\nmy.UQ\nPrograms and courses\nAcademic calendar\nStudent support\nIT support\nLibrary\nLibrary\nStudy and learning support\nResearch and publish\nVis